PROVEX patch 11-compat-pyg-seq-batches
COMPAT FIX, labelled separately: TemporalData.seq_batches() was removed in torch_geometric 2.0.4 (upstream pins 2.0.0). Use an identical seq_batches(data, batch_size) helper so that train/test run on current PyG (e.g. 2.7); batches are unchanged.
Series: upstream ProvenanceAnalytics/kairos@0e0b633beb46a1117c0a6d63be5d2481b59ac0dc DARPA/CADETS_E3, patches 01..11 applied in numeric order.
Paths are relative to DARPA/CADETS_E3: apply to a copy of kairos/upstream/ that is outside any git work tree (git apply <patch>), or from the repository root with git apply --directory=<copy dir> <patch>.

diff --git a/kairos_utils.py b/kairos_utils.py
index 429237e..c9b603b 100644
--- a/kairos_utils.py
+++ b/kairos_utils.py
@@ -239,6 +239,15 @@ def seed_arg_parser(description):
                              "(default: unseeded, upstream artifact layout)")
     return parser
 
+def seq_batches(data, batch_size):
+    """Consecutive batches of `batch_size` events of a TemporalData, in order.
+
+    Same as TemporalData.seq_batches() of torch_geometric 2.0.0 (the version
+    pinned by upstream), which was removed in torch_geometric 2.0.4.
+    """
+    for start in range(0, data.num_events, batch_size):
+        yield data[start:start + batch_size]
+
 
 
 
